<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huangchuan County</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Huangchuan County is a county in Xinyang, in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huai-river">Huai River</a> plain. Near it lie the remains of the walled capital of the ancient State of Huang, a state of the Ying clan destroyed by Chu in 648 BCE, from which the county takes its name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/huangchuan-county.jpg" alt="Huangchuan County" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Windmemories · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Huangchuan_County_aerial_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
